# Security & Configuration

## Secrets

- Store `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `PINECONE_API_KEY`, and related config in `.env`
- Ship `.env.example` with placeholder values only
- Add `.env` to `.gitignore`; never commit credentials, service accounts, or key files
- Frontend (Next.js) must not receive or store provider API keys; only `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (and similar non-secret public config) may be client-exposed

## API & data hygiene

- Validate all uploads (type, size, content) before processing
- Sanitize user query text before logging
- Prefer least-privilege Pinecone indexes/namespaces (e.g. per tenant or environment)
- Do not log raw document contents or full embeddings in production logs

## Config checklist

```
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=gemini-embedding-2-preview
GEMINI_GENERATION_MODEL=   # set explicit model id in code/config
PINECONE_API_KEY=
PINECONE_INDEX_NAME=
PINECONE_ENVIRONMENT=      # if required by client version
APP_ENV=development
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
```

## Dependency safety

- Pin versions in backend `requirements.txt` / lockfile and frontend `package.json` / lockfile
- Do not add packages without a clear need in the RAG/API or chat UI path
